The web build (web/dist, which is not in this repository) also carries the font
files that package ships in dist/prod/fonts. Each font remains under its own
license. The npm package does not include those license texts. web/licenses/fonts
has them, and web/licenses/README.md names the source of each:

  Assistant, Cascadia, Excalifont, Lilita, Nunito, Virgil, Xiaolai:
    SIL Open Font License 1.1
  ComicShanns: MIT License
  Liberation (Liberation Sans 1.05): GNU General Public License version 2,
    with the exceptions of Red Hat's Liberation font license agreement

The web build also bundles React, React Router, and the npm packages that
Excalidraw and they depend on, each under its own license. The build lists them
(web/scripts/bundled-packages.ts).

The Debian package (deploy/debian) carries CPython, built by the
python-build-standalone project, and the Python packages in uv.lock, each under
its own license. It installs the license text of every part it bundles:
/usr/share/doc/segl/copyright says where each one is.
